# RPG Battle Sim — current phase

**Stack:** Java, plain Eclipse project, package `com.battlesim`.  
**Current phase: Phase 5 in progress** (JavaFX UI on the existing engine: title, team pick, PvP, dungeon shell).  
**Source of truth:** `ROADMAP.md`. When a phase completes or design debt is paid, update both that file and this rule.

## Concept

Single-player turn-based RPG, Honkai Star Rail-style. Pre-selected teams fight enemy teams. No networking, no switching/bench — whole team fights at once. Speed-based Action Value turn order (faster characters act more often, not fixed rounds).

## Done

**Phase 1 — Core battle engine**

- `model/`: Character, Stats, Move, Type, Status, Team, CharacterTemplate, Passive
- `engine/`: TypeChart, DamageCalculator, TurnResolver, TurnOrderScheduler, StatusEffectResolver, Battle, MoveSelector, ActionChoice
- `content/`: PlayableCharacters, `content/passives/`
- `util/`: RandomProvider

**Passive system (before Phase 2)**

- `Passive` interface with default no-op hooks: `isUntargetable`, `modifyAccuracy`, `rollBonusCrit`, `modifyOutgoingDamage`, `modifyIncomingDamage`, `onHitLanded`, `onAttackMissed`, `onDamageTaken`
- `CharacterTemplate` stores `List<Supplier<Passive>>` so each battle gets fresh independent passive state
- `TurnResolver.resolveHitOnTarget` hook order: accuracy → crit → base damage → outgoing mods → incoming mods → apply damage → `onDamageTaken` → `onHitLanded` → move status chance
- `Battle` filters targets by `isUntargetable()` (e.g. Rogue stealth), with a fallback to avoid softlock

## Settled combat rules

- Bleed snapshots inflictor attack as `statusMagnitude`; ticks use 40% of that value, not the victim's attack (BLEED moves, not Champion)
- Dual Swordsman bleed snapshots 1.5× attack. Paralysis uses the default 1-turn skip on proc.
- Okirik Heal blessing (`WomanBlessingPassive`) cleanses harmful statuses (including siphon and wounds), then reduces the target's next incoming hit.
- Monk holy bonus (60% magic attack) is added after mitigation and **ignores defense** by design
- Monk Enlightenment lasts 6 turns. Divine Blessing is 100 + 8% target max HP and extends Enlightenment by 2 only after consuming 3/3 Blessed. Ult is Master of Any Art: copy the target's known kit ult (or best damaging move if they have none), retype to Holy for STAB, never miss, effects always land; 1 use if ult / 3 uses if not, then monk ult CD
- Statuses coexist (no override). Burn/poison/bleed/slow stack +15% effectiveness (duration stays). Stun/para/curse/shield/self-shield refresh to a fresh apply. All effects tick on the victim's turn.

## Upcoming

- **Phase 2 (done):** Enemy roster, boss hooks, dungeon (100 floors, boss every 15, start x0.85 then +0.20 stats every 15, rest/chest every 10, party scale 0.75/0.90/1.00), BalanceSim solo/duo/trio climb.
- **Phase 3 (done):** Starting stats ~half, XP, auto +4 HP / +1 SPD per level, +1 stat point (HP +3/+4, combat +3/+4, Speed +2/+3), 4-move ladder (1/6/12/18 ult), move points (+5 power / +5% scaling). No dungeon BST cap — players spend points freely. Sim AI even-spreads leftover points with a slight specialty bias. BalanceSim 1v1/3v3 uses Phase 2 stats.
- **Phase 4 (done):** 6-slot gear (main + 5 subs, rolls every 3 levels to +30), 2pc/4pc set bonuses, party inventory, dungeon gold/drops, console camp (sell refunds upgrade gold), rest-or-chest waypoints. BalanceSim equips drops with set-bonus priority.
- **Phase 5 (in progress):** JavaFX UI (`GuiMain`) — title, team pick, click-to-act battle with AV queue sidebar, dungeon climb with camp (equip/upgrade/sell, leftover points, rest/chest). Next: polish camp, augment skill tree, README/resume packaging.
